   {
    "t": 1794177962978,
    "text": "The Gnawhole: The side passage is narrow and wet, gnawed rather than dug. Webs hang across it in grey curtains, heavy with old husks.\n\nHalfway along, someone has set out a rug. On it, beside a small brass lamp and a chest bound in silver, sits a tall figure in a fine blue cloak, reading by the lamplight. It turns a page with one clawed hand. Its face is a tiger's, and its smile is far too polite.\n\n\"Travellers,\" it purrs, closing the book. \"How rare. I was so hoping someone would come the long way round.\"\n\nIn the webs above, something with too many legs begins to move.",
    "kind": "narrate"
   },
